WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.360
We mustache you a question — do you think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:08.160
we live in a society that can handle&nbsp;
another secret Justice League 'stache?

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.960
Well, hold on to your razors, because footage&nbsp;
from the set of Zack Snyder's Justice League&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:18.560
reshoots just leaked — and it shows that Jared&nbsp;
Leto's character once sported a very stylish strip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:23.280
of facial hair over his upper lip. Can&nbsp;
we get #releasethejokerstache trending?

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.920
For the longest time, when it came to the Justice&nbsp;
League movie, all anyone could talk about was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:33.360
mustaches. That's because Henry Cavill was&nbsp;
contractually prohibited from shaving his Mission:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.000
Impossible mustache when he did reshoots&nbsp;
for the 2017 theatrical version of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.280
and the VFX artists had to digitally remove&nbsp;
it in post-production. The effect was jarring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:49.120
and was yet one more reason so many fans wanted&nbsp;
Zack Snyder's original cut of the movie released.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.040
But as it turns out, you can't keep&nbsp;
a good 'stache down — now you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.960
add yet another digital shave to&nbsp;
your list. Here's what happened.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.960
"This is unbelievable."

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.920
Insiders tell us that Leto was thrilled about&nbsp;
Snyder's invitation to revisit the Joker role.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:09.840
Before now, he'd only been able to play the Joker&nbsp;
in 2016's Suicide Squad, but Snyder wanted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:15.520
bring him back for the his new four hour vision&nbsp;
of Justice League. To prepare for the reshoots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.880
the infamously committed method actor decided to&nbsp;
dive deep into the history of the Joker on film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:25.680
blending bits and pieces from all of the actors&nbsp;
who came before him in his own performance.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:29.440
He discovered that the very first actor&nbsp;
to play the part of the Joker — Cesar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:35.120
Romero in the 1966 Batman television&nbsp;
series — refused to shave his mustache,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.760
so the showrunners just covered it up with&nbsp;
white paint. Leto decided that the only way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:45.600
to honor him was to grow a mustache of his&nbsp;
own...but with a signature Jared Leto twist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:51.120
In a leaked excerpt from a soon-to-be-published&nbsp;
interview with Follicle Monthly, Leto said:

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:56.000
"I needed to feel the spirit of Cesar within&nbsp;
me. So I found out where he used to live in LA,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:01.600
and I used my Joker skills to break in. I stole&nbsp;
all the mustache wax and beard oil I could find,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.080
rubbing as much as I could into my own&nbsp;
mustache and drinking whatever was left.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.080
I now have the Romero essence."

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.960
"I love this guy! He's so intense!"

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.600
According to our source, when Leto showed&nbsp;
up on set, he'd already been in-character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.960
as the Joker for over a month, having applied his&nbsp;
character's makeup weeks ago and grown his dark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:32.560
bushy mustache over it, which he'd also dyed&nbsp;
green. As he got ready to shoot his scenes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:38.160
Leto explained the mustache's backstory.&nbsp;
Apparently, after Darkseid's forces took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.280
over the earth, the Joker's twisted mind&nbsp;
snapped even further. As the mustache grew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:47.280
the Joker began believing it was&nbsp;
his own sick, psycho sidekick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:52.960
which he named Harry — full name Harry Quinn.&nbsp;
He refused to shave Harry, believing his prickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:58.880
partner in crime was all that stood in the way of&nbsp;
the Earth being turned into the next Apokalips.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:03.200
Snyder, knowing better than to ask Leto&nbsp;
to break character, and having limited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.520
time to shoot the new scene, just got the&nbsp;
cameras rolling. Our sources on the set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:12.800
reportedly heard Snyder defending the actor's&nbsp;
decision to worried producers, saying, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:17.120
"I know it'll cost us another $30 million, but&nbsp;
you gotta admit — it's a pretty good joke."

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:22.320
That said, Harry wasn't the only thing that&nbsp;
hit the cutting room floor. Apparently Leto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:28.240
improvised several lines that directly referenced&nbsp;
his mustache — dialogue like, "Do you wanna know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:33.520
how I got this mustache?"; and, "Did you ever&nbsp;
try to shave a mustache in the pale moonlight?",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:39.280
and "Top this, Joaquin," and, finally,&nbsp;
"Wait'll they get a load...of this mustache."

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:44.080
Another source inside DC Comics' offices revealed&nbsp;
that Leto had actually sent the publisher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:49.680
hundreds of letters demanding that the Joker be&nbsp;
drawn with a mustache for the next ten years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.160
As of the making of this video, DC&nbsp;
still has yet to comment on our question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.600
about whether or not they might&nbsp;
want to add a little beard, too.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.480
Most interestingly, our source said that&nbsp;
since footage of the mustache-cut leaked,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:08.800
Leto has been cast in the upcoming direct-to-Quibi&nbsp;
spin-off, Mission: Impossible: Kitchen Nightmares.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.960
What do you think of this startling revelation?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.280
Are you Team Stachey, or Team&nbsp;
Shavey? Do you know what day it is?

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.779
"What a joke!"

